Fixed: FEValues computed wrong gradients and Hessians of the shape functions
of H(div) elements like FE_RaviartThomas and of FE_Nedelec on cells that are
not parallelograms if the shape function changes sign because of the face or
edge orientation: The terms coming from the derivatives of the Jacobian were
computed with the shape values that already contained the sign change, and
the sum was multiplied by the sign once more. This affected, e.g., the meshes
of GridGenerator::hyper_ball() and GridGenerator::hyper_ball_balanced().
<br>
(Richard Schussnig, 2026/11/20)
